# =============================================================================
#  ISPFlow - FreeRADIUS `post-auth` policy (session opening).
#
#  INLINED into the site's `post-auth { }` section by install-vps.sh. See the
#  header of the `authorize` file for why inlining is required and what every
#  other mechanism does instead.
#
#  Runs after a successful authentication and turns a login into a usable,
#  billable session: it opens an accounting session in ISPFlow so the panel can
#  show who is online, for how long, and through which router.
#
#  Idempotent on acct_session_id, so a router that re-sends Acct-Start on a link
#  flap updates one row instead of creating a second session and double counting
#  the customer's online time.
#
#  ------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Why this section contains no `if`
#  ------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Neither `post-auth { }` nor `accounting { }` accepts a top-level conditional
#  in FreeRADIUS 3.2.5:
#
#      sites-enabled/default: Invalid location for 'if'
#
#  Only `authorize { }` and `authenticate { }` are full unlang sections. An `if`
#  in either of the other two is a startup failure, not a runtime one, so the
#  decision that would have been made there is made in SQL instead, which is
#  where it belongs: the INSERT ... SELECT matches no row for an unregistered
#  router or an unknown subscriber, and writes nothing.
# =============================================================================

# Invoking the module IS the call: in the post-auth section rlm_sql runs the
# `post-auth { query }` statement from queries.conf. There is no sql_query()
# function in FreeRADIUS 3.
#
# The statement derives isp_id from radius_nas by Called-Station-Id and joins the
# subscriber inside that tenant, so an unregistered router inserts nothing and a
# second ISP's identically named customer can never be opened by the wrong
# router.
#
# A failure here must NOT reject a customer who has already authenticated. The
# router has admitted them; refusing now would cut a paying customer off because
# of a bookkeeping problem. The panel shows the session as soon as the first
# Interim-Update lands.
sql